{"title":"1970 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Find all number triples <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/3/c73ed093cc73a8d9a14185fa525e7067e5c3725d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y,z)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"58\" height=\"18\" /> such that when any of these numbers is added to the product of the other two, the result is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/c/41c544263a265ff15498ee45f7392c5f86c6d151.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>We have:\n</p>\n<center>\n<p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/2/2/522004cf02626d17b2b43ac70f94dfa4a2242d01.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\begin{matrix} x + yz &amp;=&amp; 2\\\\ y + xz &amp;=&amp; 2\\\\ z + yx &amp;=&amp; 2 \\end{matrix}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -23px\" width=\"107\" height=\"55\" />\n</p>\n</center>\n<p>From the first equation minus the second, we get&#160;:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/2/0/620c8551cdc003c897cd60e620e0f6a453f94137.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{matrix}x-y + yz - xz &amp;=&amp; 0 \\\\(1-z)(x-y) &amp;=&amp; 0\\end{matrix}\\]\" width=\"180\" height=\"37\" />\n</p><p>So either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/d/6bd3d68e77a39e1ea97e7009f70e12622fa76835.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" /> or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/1/0110f1bb04c51b2a4d431bf14489fc1b48b37421.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"11\" />. For <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/b/d/6bd3d68e77a39e1ea97e7009f70e12622fa76835.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$z=1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"41\" height=\"12\" />, since the equations were symmetric, we have one solution of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/e/0/be0934bc275d55cdaaa1a44959370defba39e808.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$(x,y,z)=(1,1,1)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"139\" height=\"18\" />.\nFrom <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/1/1/0110f1bb04c51b2a4d431bf14489fc1b48b37421.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=y$\" style=\"vertical-align: -3px\" width=\"43\" height=\"11\" />, substituting it into the original three derived equations, we have:\n<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/6/c/f6c4322d96e4d83b378519dfe13c679f43644cc6.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{matrix} x+xz &amp;=&amp; 2\\\\ z + x^2 &amp;=&amp; 2 \\end{matrix}\\]\" width=\"107\" height=\"33\" />\nWe then get <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/d/6/fd6381d3040210d943035e8fd4b7f2388c689814.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[z = 2-x^2\\]\" width=\"81\" height=\"15\" /> Substituting this into <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/0/6/206d5d6d817265f8ef6ab68cef2ca6cc3f5d2de0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x+xz = 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"85\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/c/8/4c86c53830aec8163507f4db372088fda15fbaa2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[\\begin{matrix} x + x(2-x^2) &amp;=&amp; 2\\\\ x^3 - 3x + 2 &amp;=&amp; 0\\\\ (x-1)^2(x+2) = 0 \\end{matrix}\\]\" width=\"207\" height=\"58\" />\nThus, either <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/4/3/34310f2f36ed6d724838edb08788ee62acb33386.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = 1$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, or <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/6/f361efa9ea92a34219e05e0825907161f273f17a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x = -2$\" width=\"57\" height=\"12\" />. Since the equations were symmetric, we then get the full solution set of:\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/2/4/324fe63375a7dbda6240c2f1ee0e19c97973e8f2.png\" class=\"latexcenter\" alt=\"\\[(x,y,z) = {(1,1,1), (-2,-2,-2)}\\]\" width=\"246\" height=\"18\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_Canadian_MO\" title=\"1970 Canadian MO\">1970 Canadian MO</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_Canadian_MO_Problems\" title=\"1970 Canadian MO Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b>First Question</b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"34%\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1970 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_3\" title=\"1970 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"1970 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"1970 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"1970 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"1970 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"1970 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_9\" title=\"1970 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"1970 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 10\">10</a>\n</td>\n<td width=\"33%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1970_Canadian_MO_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"1970 Canadian MO Problems/Problem 2\">Problem 2</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261016190137\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: []\nCPU time usage: 0.023 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.121 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 116/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 986/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 68/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 3036/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   10.605      1 Template:Old_CanadaMO_box\n100.00%   10.605      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:10532:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261016190137 and revision id 50407. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}